VPNonly — licensing
===================

This repository holds two different kinds of material, under two different
terms. Read this before copying anything out of it.

MIT licensed — the terms below apply in full:

  * The command-line tool at the repository root: up.sh, down.sh, run.sh,
    status.sh, fetch-creds.sh, parse-wg.py and vpnrun.c
  * Everything under app-engine/, which is the privileged source that runs
    as root inside the VPNonly app

All rights reserved — the MIT terms below do NOT apply:

  * The compiled VPNonly application, distributed as VPNonly-*.zip under
    docs/ and as GitHub release assets. It is a paid product; redistributing
    it is not permitted. Its terms of use are at https://vpnonly.app/terms.html
  * The website under docs/ — its pages, stylesheets, images and video

Bundled WireGuard and Sparkle components keep their own upstream licences.
See app-engine/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt for those notices.

If you want to read, audit, modify or reuse the part of VPNonly that runs with
root privileges, that is the MIT-licensed material above, and you are welcome
to it.

